# monitoring-hub offline bundle

Self-contained package repository. Copy this directory to the air-gapped host,
then add the local repo and install — no network required.

Verify integrity first: `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`
{% if signed %}
The repository metadata is GPG-signed; import the bundled key before installing.
{% endif %}
{% if rpm_targets %}
## RHEL / EL (dnf)
{% for t in rpm_targets %}
### {{ t.target }} ({{ t.arch }})

```sh
cd "$(dirname "$0")"
{% if signed %}sudo rpm --import RPM-GPG-KEY-monitoring-hub
{% endif %}sudo tee /etc/yum.repos.d/mh-offline.repo >/dev/null <<EOF
[mh-offline]
name=mh-offline
baseurl=file://$PWD/yum/{{ t.target }}/{{ t.arch }}
enabled=1
gpgcheck=0
repo_gpgcheck={{ 1 if signed else 0 }}
{% if signed %}gpgkey=file://$PWD/RPM-GPG-KEY-monitoring-hub
{% endif %}EOF
# air-gapped: consult ONLY the bundle repo (the distro's default repos are offline)
sudo dnf -y --disablerepo='*' --enablerepo=mh-offline install <package>
```
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
